  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING - FileArtifactReference.Observed() is removed, and teardown now deletes files a run discovered. FileArtifactFolderFinder previously marked its results observed, so a discovered file was never deleted; now it is an ordinary file reference and the timeline decides. Chain MarkReadonly() onto the FindArtifact / FindArtifacts call for a folder the run only reads. Requires TestFramework.Core 0.3.0.\nWhat to change: replace Observed() with MarkReadonly() on the declaring call. A timeline that discovers files in a folder it does not own - a build output directory, a shared drop location - must add MarkReadonly() before upgrading, or teardown will delete those files.\nFiles the run creates itself, through UseRunDirectory() or SetupArtifact, are unaffected: they were removed at teardown before and still are.",
